This mismatch happens because of a small gap in the backend logic: when the Creator submits a batch (especially via Bulk Upload), the Java backend sometimes forgets to save the SCHEDULED_TIME into the VOUCHER_WORKFLOW history table for that specific step.
Because the SCHEDULED_TIME is missing for that specific row in the history list, the frontend assumes it wasn't scheduled and defaults to showing the **"Immediate Execution"** chip.
We can easily fix this entirely on the frontend! We will tell the code: *"If the history log doesn't have a time, but this is the Submission step and the batch itself has a scheduled time, grab the time from the batch details!"*
Here is the exact fix for **VoucherPostingStatus.js** (You should also apply this to VoucherAuthorization.js so they match perfectly).
